WEBVTT

00:01.117 --> 00:03.017
Let's see, what else?

00:03.086 --> 00:06.180
Okay. Here's one of the first things
your uncle Charlie wrote.

00:07.157 --> 00:10.923
&lt;i>Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles&lt;/i>

00:16.166 --> 00:17.292
What do you think?

00:17.834 --> 00:19.563
Must have been before my time.

00:23.106 --> 00:24.664
Okay, we're done here.

00:26.509 --> 00:30.138
Don't put your juice box on the piano,
it leaves a ring.

00:30.613 --> 00:32.478
How could a box leave a ring?

00:34.184 --> 00:35.617
Got to run to the grocery store.

00:35.685 --> 00:37.812
I'm gonna need somebody
to fold these clothes.

00:37.921 --> 00:39.445
I don't know if the grocery store

00:39.522 --> 00:41.683
is the first place I'd go for that,
but good luck.

00:42.459 --> 00:46.190
Remember, you're being punished.
So, no TV, no computer, no GameBoy.

00:46.296 --> 00:47.957
I need you to be my eyes and ears.

00:48.031 --> 00:50.591
Okay, but you have to be
my liver and prostate.

00:53.103 --> 00:54.866
Whoa, whose is this?

00:57.006 --> 00:59.031
Charlie, you want to field that one?

00:59.142 --> 01:03.101
No problem. Jake, sometimes when you
have a casual sexual relationship...

01:03.179 --> 01:04.771
All right!

01:06.683 --> 01:10.210
Jake, we take in strangers' laundry
because we're poor.

01:11.788 --> 01:14.518
I'll be back in an hour.
Start folding. No TV.

01:19.028 --> 01:20.393
What'd you get busted for?

01:20.497 --> 01:22.124
I painted my room at Mom's house.

01:22.198 --> 01:24.666
- What's wrong with that?
- I'm 10 years old.

01:28.571 --> 01:31.335
- How about a little sock golf?
- What's that?

01:32.008 --> 01:33.873
Okay, here's how it works.

01:33.977 --> 01:36.207
The living room is a dogleg par four.

01:37.881 --> 01:40.975
That means you have to get your sock
into the kitchen sink

01:41.050 --> 01:43.075
- in four strokes or less.
- Okay.

01:43.486 --> 01:45.215
We'll play for a quarter a hole.

01:46.723 --> 01:48.020
Your handicap's obvious.

01:48.091 --> 01:50.924
You're short, and you've never
heard of the Ninja Turtles.

01:51.294 --> 01:53.262
All right, keep your knees bent.

01:53.763 --> 01:56.095
Your arm straight and swing easy.

02:00.970 --> 02:02.767
Oh, man, I'm being hustled.

02:03.239 --> 02:05.867
- We can play for less if you want.
- Don't get cocky.

02:07.443 --> 02:09.035
There's 17 more holes.

02:18.121 --> 02:21.056
The 18th hole, all square.

02:21.658 --> 02:25.185
The defending champion looks
to have an easy tap-in for a birdie

02:25.428 --> 02:28.829
as the gallery waits breathlessly
for the rookie to respond.

02:29.465 --> 02:31.296
Would you please stop talking?

02:33.503 --> 02:35.937
Tempers flare as the pressure mounts.

02:41.477 --> 02:43.741
- Yeah.
- It's unbelievable.

02:43.847 --> 02:45.337
An eagle on the 18th.

02:45.448 --> 02:48.349
This has never happened before
in the history of sock golf!

02:48.451 --> 02:49.782
A little help here?

02:49.853 --> 02:52.845
Fans are coming out of the gallery
with sacks of groceries

02:52.922 --> 02:55.186
- for the young phenom.
- What's going on?

02:55.425 --> 02:57.222
I won. I beat Uncle Charlie.

02:57.293 --> 02:59.887
Excuse me, didn't I ask you
to fold the laundry?

02:59.963 --> 03:02.431
Laundry? Are you barking mad?

03:02.532 --> 03:05.865
The child just won the coveted
Palmolive Cup.

03:06.102 --> 03:09.469
I won. You lose.

03:10.340 --> 03:12.672
When I ask Jake to do something,

03:12.742 --> 03:14.642
I need you to help me
make sure he does it.

03:14.711 --> 03:16.770
I'm trying to teach him responsibility.

03:17.280 --> 03:19.180
This sock is soaking wet.

03:19.282 --> 03:22.945
Yeah, I chipped into the water hazard
on the ninth and the lid was open.

03:23.953 --> 03:26.683
- So, this is toilet water?
- At least.

03:34.697 --> 03:37.598
All right.
I put Jake to bed, I folded the laundry,

03:37.667 --> 03:39.134
I put the groceries away...

03:39.202 --> 03:41.363
The guilt thing doesn't work on me, Alan.

03:41.671 --> 03:44.606
Yeah, well, it's all I got.
I'll be back in a little while.

03:45.174 --> 03:48.268
- Where you going?
- I have to bring the garbage cans back in.

03:48.511 --> 03:50.001
Today wasn't garbage day.

03:50.213 --> 03:53.273
- No, not here. At Judith's.
- At Judith's?

03:54.517 --> 03:56.951
Alan, your wife threw you out.

03:57.020 --> 03:59.352
Yeah, that doesn't mean
she doesn't need me.

03:59.422 --> 04:01.083
Yeah, it kind of does.

04:02.759 --> 04:06.627
Look, we're still married,
it's still my house,

04:06.696 --> 04:08.960
and she still counts on me
to do a few chores.

04:09.032 --> 04:12.524
It's good. It leaves the door open for,
you know, reconciliation.

04:13.136 --> 04:14.398
I see.

04:14.704 --> 04:18.470
So, how do you lift those garbage cans
without a spine?

04:23.713 --> 04:25.078
They're on wheels.

04:34.490 --> 04:36.082
What are you watching?

04:37.260 --> 04:38.852
I'm watching a movie,

04:38.928 --> 04:41.328
and you're not supposed
to be watching anything.

04:41.431 --> 04:42.762
Oh, yeah.

04:43.132 --> 04:46.363
- Is that guy a good guy or a bad guy?
- Good guy.

04:47.170 --> 04:49.331
And you're not supposed
to be watching TV.

04:49.605 --> 04:50.833
I know.

04:54.844 --> 04:57.312
- Is that his girlfriend?
- Ex-girlfriend.

04:58.014 --> 04:59.675
But he still loves her, right?

04:59.816 --> 05:02.376
I'm not going to walk you
through the whole movie.

05:03.686 --> 05:04.983
I think so.

05:06.189 --> 05:08.783
- Go to bed, Jake.
- Okay.

05:12.695 --> 05:13.821
Who's that guy?

05:13.896 --> 05:15.625
That's the guy he was in jail with

05:15.698 --> 05:17.563
and told him
where the money was hidden.

05:17.633 --> 05:19.066
Right.

05:19.869 --> 05:23.305
- You're being punished. No TV.
- I know.

05:32.348 --> 05:34.043
What the hell is going on?

05:35.985 --> 05:37.680
- Jake?
- Goodnight.

05:42.091 --> 05:43.649
Hey, I'm watching that.

05:43.726 --> 05:45.956
What part of "no TV"
didn't you understand?

05:46.029 --> 05:47.826
I'm allowed to watch TV.

05:48.164 --> 05:49.392
I mean Jake.

05:49.499 --> 05:52.957
I said, "No TV." He said, "Okay. "
I said, "Go to bed. " He said, "Okay. "

05:53.036 --> 05:55.800
- What'd you want from me?
- He's taking advantage of you

05:55.872 --> 05:57.533
because he knows
you won't follow through.

05:57.607 --> 05:59.768
He obviously knows me
better than you do.

06:00.710 --> 06:03.645
If this is gonna work out
with Jake living here part-time,

06:03.713 --> 06:06.375
you have to be an adult.
You have to impose discipline.

06:06.449 --> 06:08.610
Yeah, fine, whatever.
Give me back the remote.

06:08.718 --> 06:11.243
No. You're not listening to me.
You need to be firm.

06:11.320 --> 06:12.719
Okay.

06:13.723 --> 06:16.453
- Go to your room.
- Yes, like that.

06:16.826 --> 06:19.818
I mean it. Give me the remote
and go to your room.

06:19.929 --> 06:21.226
That's very funny.

06:21.964 --> 06:24.660
I'm serious. Get out of here,
or I will kick your ass.

06:33.910 --> 06:35.343
Oh, man.

06:49.959 --> 06:51.187
Shoo.

07:03.806 --> 07:05.171
Jake.

07:07.009 --> 07:08.601
It was on when I came in.

07:11.981 --> 07:13.141
Yeah, right.

07:13.616 --> 07:16.483
What did I tell you about leaving
juice boxes on my piano?

07:16.719 --> 07:18.152
How do you know it's mine?

07:20.223 --> 07:24.785
Come on, who else around here drinks
"Transylvania Goofy Juice"?

07:25.995 --> 07:27.121
Good point.

07:28.865 --> 07:32.164
And another thing. Were you on the deck
feeding the seagulls again?

07:32.235 --> 07:33.702
Sorry, I forgot.

07:35.238 --> 07:38.002
Okay. We need to talk.

07:39.575 --> 07:41.167
Love you, Uncle Charlie.

07:42.411 --> 07:45.574
Look, we don't feed the seagulls
because you can't get rid of them.

07:45.681 --> 07:47.546
We don't leave
the doors and windows open,

07:47.617 --> 07:50.484
because we get all kinds of bugs
and crap flying in the house.

07:50.553 --> 07:52.953
- Okay.
- No. Don't just say "okay. "

07:53.022 --> 07:55.513
This is not the grownup
telling the kid what to do.

07:55.591 --> 07:58.116
This is just two guys agreeing
how to live together.

07:58.227 --> 08:00.058
- Are we cool?
- Yeah. Cool.

08:02.565 --> 08:04.362
- What's going on?
- Nothing.

08:04.734 --> 08:06.599
- Was he watching TV?
- No.

08:09.372 --> 08:11.863
Jake, I have to run a quick errand.

08:11.941 --> 08:15.377
Why don't you wash and dress?
When I get back, we'll do something fun.

08:15.444 --> 08:17.036
- Can we watch TV?
- Go.

08:20.416 --> 08:21.815
Where are you off to?

08:22.818 --> 08:24.809
The grocery store.

08:30.259 --> 08:33.751
- You're going to Judith's, aren't you?
- No.

08:35.765 --> 08:37.392
Then where are you going?

08:38.401 --> 08:39.732
Judith's.

08:41.137 --> 08:42.764
- Alan.
- I have to.

08:42.838 --> 08:46.171
The timer on the sprinkler system
is broken,

08:46.275 --> 08:49.972
and the flower beds are getting flooded,
and I love her and I want her back.

08:51.013 --> 08:52.810
Buddy, I feel for you.

08:53.416 --> 08:56.112
- Thank you.
- Unfortunately, the feeling is nausea.

08:58.754 --> 09:00.745
Great. I'll see you later.

09:00.923 --> 09:03.790
Alan, you've been making
the same mistake your whole life.

09:03.859 --> 09:07.351
Being the good boy, fixing everything
so everybody would love you.

09:07.463 --> 09:08.794
It didn't work with Mom.

09:08.864 --> 09:11.731
It didn't work with either of the women
you went out with.

09:12.468 --> 09:14.299
And it's not gonna work with your wife.

09:14.370 --> 09:19.330
You know nothing about commitment
and responsibility to a relationship.

09:19.875 --> 09:22.469
Granted. But I do know
when a woman's using me.

09:22.745 --> 09:24.679
And by that I mean not in a fun way.

09:25.581 --> 09:28.379
Well, you can rest easy,
because no one is using me.

09:31.587 --> 09:34.988
And did you mean that I only dated
two women including Judith?

09:35.925 --> 09:38.758
Because if you did,
I have two words for you.

09:40.529 --> 09:41.996
Maxine Chernakoff.

09:55.778 --> 09:59.077
- Did you fix it?
- Not quite.

09:59.148 --> 10:01.139
It doesn't seem like
you're changing anything.

10:01.250 --> 10:04.845
No? Well, sometimes change happens,
Judith, and you can't see it.

10:07.123 --> 10:09.216
Okay. Fine. When you're done fixing this,

10:09.292 --> 10:11.783
would you come and take a look
at the garbage disposal?

10:11.894 --> 10:13.327
- Sure.
- Thank you.

10:14.897 --> 10:16.262
Wait, no.

10:18.301 --> 10:19.563
What?

10:20.069 --> 10:22.970
No, I won't come inside
and look at the garbage disposal.

10:23.606 --> 10:25.005
Why not?

10:27.476 --> 10:30.570
I know when I'm being used, Judith,
and not in a fun way.

10:31.580 --> 10:33.013
What are you talking about?

10:33.115 --> 10:35.743
Who are we kidding? The marriage is over.

10:35.851 --> 10:39.252
You're just afraid to move on,
so, you keep dragging me over here,

10:39.322 --> 10:41.620
and I'm afraid to move on,
so I keep coming.

10:44.894 --> 10:47.556
Goodbye, Judith. You're free.

10:48.397 --> 10:51.491
I hope you find
whatever it is you're looking for.

11:06.215 --> 11:08.649
- What you got there?
- Just a little bread.

11:09.585 --> 11:12.315
Please tell me you're not feeding
the seagulls again.

11:14.857 --> 11:16.051
Okay.

11:17.860 --> 11:21.523
Man, did you let another one of those
big flappy bastards in the house?

11:21.864 --> 11:24.992
You have to put $1 in the swear jar,
you said "bastards. "

11:25.067 --> 11:26.728
Smart, poke the bear.

11:28.070 --> 11:30.197
I'm telling you, Jake, this is the last...

11:34.610 --> 11:36.043
Yikes!

11:40.916 --> 11:42.645
I'm really sorry, Uncle Charlie.

11:42.752 --> 11:44.720
I don't want to talk to you right now.

11:44.820 --> 11:48.881
Hello, do you have a department
of animal control or bird abatement?

11:50.993 --> 11:52.722
I have a seagull problem.

11:53.729 --> 11:55.128
Seagull.

11:56.632 --> 11:58.122
Thank you, I'll hold.

11:58.234 --> 12:00.065
I didn't know there'd be so many.

12:00.403 --> 12:04.305
I told you, don't feed the damn things.
I told you, don't leave the windows open.

12:04.407 --> 12:06.170
Yeah, hi, who's this?

12:07.143 --> 12:08.633
Phyllis Siegal.

12:16.986 --> 12:21.047
No, Phyllis, I wanted to talk to somebody
about seagulls.

12:21.957 --> 12:23.982
I got a flock of seagulls in my house.

12:25.361 --> 12:27.625
No, I don't know
whatever happened to them.

12:28.531 --> 12:30.055
I'm really sorry.

12:30.366 --> 12:32.857
We had an agreement, Jake,
and you broke it.

12:32.968 --> 12:36.802
Look, I need somebody who can come over
with a net or something.

12:38.207 --> 12:39.572
Sure, I'll hold.

12:40.176 --> 12:41.973
Hello? Who's this?

12:42.912 --> 12:44.311
Annette.

12:47.016 --> 12:50.679
Look, I got a room
filled with seagulls and... No.

12:53.355 --> 12:54.822
Hi, Phyllis.

12:55.558 --> 12:57.025
Goodbye, Phyllis.

12:57.159 --> 12:58.387
Good news.

12:58.928 --> 13:01.260
Really? Come tell me in Jake's room.

13:01.530 --> 13:04.192
What did he do?
He didn't paint anything, did he?

13:04.533 --> 13:06.194
I want you to be surprised.

13:08.704 --> 13:11.605
You will never guess what happened
while I was at Judith's.

13:12.241 --> 13:13.674
Neither will you.

13:15.711 --> 13:17.235
Oh, my God!

13:17.746 --> 13:19.611
So, what's your good news?

13:20.449 --> 13:21.711
Open the door!

13:22.218 --> 13:25.278
Your kid got them in there,
you get them out.

13:25.387 --> 13:28.151
Open the door!

13:34.063 --> 13:35.724
That was not funny, Charlie.

13:37.299 --> 13:39.597
&lt;i>Depends on what side of the door
you were on:&lt;/i>

13:40.803 --> 13:43.169
Look, I'm really sorry about the birds,

13:43.239 --> 13:45.503
but I'm sure they'll leave
as soon as they get hungry.

13:45.574 --> 13:47.269
That's what I thought about you.

13:47.576 --> 13:50.841
You know what? Jake and I may be
out of here sooner than you think.

13:50.946 --> 13:53.847
- What do you mean?
- At Judith's, there was kissing.

13:54.416 --> 13:57.943
Mutual kissing. Unprompted,
but reciprocated by yours truly.

13:58.787 --> 14:00.015
Wow.

14:00.122 --> 14:01.851
And was it as boring as it sounds?

14:02.992 --> 14:04.516
Charlie, she kissed me.

14:04.593 --> 14:08.461
This wasn't the kiss of a woman who just
wanted her garbage disposal unclogged.

14:09.899 --> 14:12.697
Well, you know her plumbing
better than I do.

14:12.801 --> 14:15.702
You know what I'm gonna do?
I'm gonna let her come to me.

14:16.472 --> 14:18.997
You know, be detached,
play it cool. You know?

14:19.074 --> 14:21.042
Yeah. That's your home-run swing.

14:22.811 --> 14:25.507
Hey, Uncle Charlie,
you want to play some sock golf?

14:26.215 --> 14:28.080
- No, thanks.
- Where are you going?

14:28.584 --> 14:29.846
I'm going for a drive.

14:29.919 --> 14:31.477
- Can I come?
- Nope.

14:35.991 --> 14:38.391
I don't think
Uncle Charlie likes me anymore.

14:39.395 --> 14:42.421
Don't be silly.
He's just a little upset about the 30, 40

14:42.498 --> 14:44.523
screaming, crapping birds in his house.

14:44.867 --> 14:47.995
Why don't you write him a note
and tell him how sorry you are?

14:48.170 --> 14:49.262
Okay.

14:50.439 --> 14:52.339
Don't worry, he'll come around.

14:53.242 --> 14:55.642
Sooner or later, everybody comes around.

14:57.146 --> 15:01.446
You just have to give them a little time
and a little space.

15:03.619 --> 15:04.881
Hello, Judith?

15:10.225 --> 15:12.750
- What's in the bucket?
- Chum.

15:15.230 --> 15:16.959
- What?
- Bait.

15:17.933 --> 15:21.391
I went down to the bait shop
and asked them what seagulls like to eat.

15:21.470 --> 15:22.767
We're keeping them?

15:23.405 --> 15:25.930
No. We're gonna throw the bait
out the window

15:26.008 --> 15:27.908
to lure the birds out of the house.

15:27.977 --> 15:29.467
That's pretty clever.

15:30.279 --> 15:33.806
Yeah, it's a variation on something I do
with women and tennis bracelets.

15:36.318 --> 15:38.411
Hey, Uncle Charlie, I made this for you.

15:44.526 --> 15:45.788
Thanks.

15:46.462 --> 15:47.793
I made it myself.

15:48.731 --> 15:49.993
I see that.

15:51.834 --> 15:54.394
- What are you doing?
- I'm getting rid of the birds.

15:54.503 --> 15:56.027
- Can I help?
- Nope.

15:57.306 --> 16:00.400
Jake, why don't you go out
and play on the deck, okay?

16:00.509 --> 16:01.806
Okay.

16:05.681 --> 16:07.205
What is wrong with you?

16:07.316 --> 16:10.012
He worked really hard on that card.
You barely looked at it.

16:10.085 --> 16:13.179
- What do you want from me?
- He's dying for you to forgive him.

16:13.255 --> 16:15.314
Fine. I forgive him.

16:15.758 --> 16:19.057
Now, are you gonna help me or not?
I got a serious problem here.

16:21.030 --> 16:23.726
Really? Because you look like
you have it all together.

16:25.200 --> 16:26.997
Okay, here's the deal.

16:28.671 --> 16:31.834
We go in there and start throwing
this stuff out the windows.

16:31.940 --> 16:33.339
When the last bird's out,

16:33.409 --> 16:36.435
we close the window
and get on with our lives.

16:36.545 --> 16:37.842
You're ready?

16:39.481 --> 16:40.778
Sure.

16:41.283 --> 16:45.344
You know, if they love this bait so much,
why would they even wait for...

16:58.634 --> 17:00.795
It's almost like somebody tipped them off.

17:01.637 --> 17:03.798
- You got any other bright ideas?
- Yeah.

17:04.473 --> 17:07.465
I'm gonna get a drywall guy in there
and seal off that room.

17:08.644 --> 17:11.477
- Very funny.
- I'm not kidding.

17:12.147 --> 17:13.637
That room is dead to me.

17:15.751 --> 17:17.412
Either that or sell the house.

17:18.120 --> 17:20.816
I'll put it on the market
as a two bedroom plus aviary.

17:22.157 --> 17:23.784
Everybody loves an aviary.

17:25.360 --> 17:26.554
What about Jake?

17:26.662 --> 17:29.495
Are you gonna put him on the market
or just wall him off?

17:29.565 --> 17:31.123
I tried with that kid, Alan.

17:31.200 --> 17:33.828
He says one thing,
and then he goes and does another.

17:33.902 --> 17:36.735
He's 10. He's got the attention span
of a hummingbird.

17:37.639 --> 17:39.800
What am I supposed to do
when he ignores me?

17:39.875 --> 17:43.072
You punish him. You take away
his computer, his TV, his toys.

17:43.178 --> 17:44.873
You already took away all the good stuff.

17:44.980 --> 17:47.676
What am I supposed to take away?
His bronchial inhaler?

17:47.916 --> 17:51.249
You know what I'm saying, Charlie.
You don't take away your love.

18:39.134 --> 18:42.297
Hi. I tried calling
but I kept getting your machine,

18:42.404 --> 18:45.100
- so I thought I'd bring this over.
- What is it?

18:45.174 --> 18:49.577
It's my master file of handymen, plumbers,
electricians, maintenance schedules,

18:49.645 --> 18:52.239
warranties, authorized repair centers,

18:52.848 --> 18:54.247
et cetera.

18:54.983 --> 18:57.611
Okay, well, you're on your own.
Got to run.

18:58.387 --> 18:59.649
Alan, wait.

19:03.492 --> 19:06.290
- Yes?
- About that kiss?

19:09.064 --> 19:12.625
When you said we should move on,
I got scared, and...

19:13.836 --> 19:15.633
Alan, I kissed you out of fear.

19:16.538 --> 19:17.869
Hey, it still counts.

19:19.241 --> 19:21.539
Alan, you were right. We have to move on.

19:22.878 --> 19:24.004
Okay.

19:25.747 --> 19:27.305
Alan, wait.

19:31.987 --> 19:33.079
Yes?

19:33.188 --> 19:35.816
The garbage disposal's still making
that horrible noise.

19:35.891 --> 19:38.223
I keep telling you not to put bones in it.

19:38.493 --> 19:41.018
- I didn't.
- The sink trap does not lie, Judith.

19:43.732 --> 19:46.064
This is so cool, Uncle Charlie.

19:46.368 --> 19:49.701
Yeah, I was kind of hard on you,
and I wanted to make it up.

19:50.706 --> 19:52.765
So, you're not still mad
about the seagulls?

19:52.875 --> 19:56.072
I'm still mad. I just figured out
a better way to deal with it.

19:56.311 --> 19:58.575
Well, I think this is a very good way.

20:00.983 --> 20:02.245
Me, too.

20:02.651 --> 20:04.016
I'm buying you all this stuff,

20:04.086 --> 20:07.419
but as punishment for letting seagulls
in my house,

20:07.489 --> 20:09.389
you can't play with it for a month.

20:09.458 --> 20:10.891
A month?

20:11.093 --> 20:12.617
Pretty smart, huh?

20:13.595 --> 20:15.153
It's not fair.

20:16.431 --> 20:17.898
You know what this is?

20:18.333 --> 20:20.233
The world's smallest violin.

20:23.672 --> 20:25.139
What are you talking about?

20:35.017 --> 20:36.484
They're gone, Charlie.

20:38.320 --> 20:40.652
Are you sure? Check under the bed.

20:44.359 --> 20:45.451
All clear.

20:46.461 --> 20:47.792
Okay.

20:48.664 --> 20:50.029
I wonder why they left.

20:50.132 --> 20:52.066
Maybe because we stopped feeding them.

20:53.735 --> 20:55.225
Whoa, check it out.

20:58.840 --> 21:00.171
Wow.

21:00.842 --> 21:03.242
- You know what this means, don't you?
- Yeah.

21:03.879 --> 21:05.039
Breakfast.

21:31.239 --> 21:32.433
English

00:00.500 --> 00:02.000
&lt;font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net&lt;/font>
